  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「センニンサボテン」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%BB%E3%83%B3%E3%83%8B%E3%83%B3%E3%82%B5%E3%83%9C%E3%83%86%E3%83%B3",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 106365669,
      "text": "センニンサボテン は、サボテン科に分類されるサボテンの一種。アメリカ大陸原産だが、ヨーロッパやアフリカ、オーストラリア、日本などの世界各地に定着しており、侵略的な外来種として問題になっている。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Opuntia stricta」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Opuntia_stricta",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1352056093,
      "text": "Opuntia stricta is a species of large cactus that is native to subtropical and tropical coastal areas of the Americas, especially around the Caribbean and the lower East Coast of the United States. Common names include erect prickly pear and nopal estricto (Spanish). The first description as Cactus strictus was published in 1803 by Adrian Hardy Haworth. In 1812 he moved the species to the genus Opuntia."
    }
  },
